<title>SPAIN: Spain's Metrovacesa H1 pre-tax rises 14 pct.</title>
<headline>Spain's Metrovacesa H1 pre-tax rises 14 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results for Spanish property firm Metrovacesa in billions of pesetas, unless stated:</p>
<p> Pretax profit			     4.29   vs   3.78</p>
<p> Net taxed				   3.00   vs   2.87</p>
<p> Rental income			     4.10   up   6.8 pct</p>
<p> Cashflow				    4.63   up   6.7 pct</p>
<p> Sales margin				2.89   up  28.8 pct</p>
<p>NOTE: Metrovacesa said the pace of rental income growth would speed up in the coming months with rents from new spaces like the Torre de Madrid expected, and a decrease of vacant square metres, especially in offices. The percent of unoccupied rentable space has fallen to 6.3 percent compared with 9.9 percent in December 1996.</p>
</text>
